WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.636
The service has not launched, so operating revenue is currently zero.

00:00:04.666 --> 00:00:09.226
The six-year figures are an internal model built from stated assumptions.

00:00:09.256 --> 00:00:13.023
They are planning targets, not forecasts guaranteed to occur.

00:00:13.123 --> 00:00:18.277
Initial support revenue uses four inputs: users, support rate, frequency, and price.

00:00:18.307 --> 00:00:23.460
One support payment is three thousand yen and includes five commemorative pieces.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:28.223
The model counts support payments, not the number of pieces distributed.

00:00:28.323 --> 00:00:33.481
The first revenue plan combines preservation support and seller purchase referral fees.

00:00:33.511 --> 00:00:37.797
The first table assumes no income from referral fees.

00:00:37.827 --> 00:00:42.550
Management forecasts exclude sponsor prize funds. Financial reporting follows each contract.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:47.520
After results are verified, a later phase may add advertising placement fees.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:53.551
Card and data revenue require IP rights, user consent, privacy protection, and verified utility.

00:00:53.581 --> 00:00:58.298
Fees from paid resale or cash-based prediction remain undecided future options.

00:00:58.398 --> 00:01:01.824
The base model reaches operating break-even in 2028.

00:01:01.854 --> 00:01:06.574
Break-even is planned for 2028. Operating profit is planned for 2029.

00:01:06.604 --> 00:01:11.746
Cost, timing, user growth, and support behavior can move that date materially.

00:01:11.846 --> 00:01:14.798
Four planned financing rounds are shown in yen.

00:01:14.828 --> 00:01:19.978
Each later round requires product, user, rights, audit, legal, and profit gates.

00:01:20.008 --> 00:01:24.648
If a target is missed, the next round is delayed or reduced.

00:01:24.748 --> 00:01:29.903
The one-trillion-yen figure is a long-term scenario, not the 2032 base plan.

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:35.853
Ten million users buy support 2.8 times a month. Each purchase costs 3,000 yen.

00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:41.136
Multiplying those assumptions by twelve months gives one point zero zero eight trillion yen.

00:01:41.236 --> 00:01:46.389
Investor ownership depends on financing terms, company valuation, and future share issuance.

00:01:46.419 --> 00:01:51.513
The conversion price has a cap. This does not guarantee principal or returns.

00:01:51.543 --> 00:01:55.410
IPO timing, future valuation, and investor liquidity remain uncertain.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:59.373
The model becomes useful when actual data replaces assumptions.

00:01:59.403 --> 00:02:04.603
The team will track acquisition cost, retention, support behavior, and sponsor renewal.

00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:09.783
The next financing decision should follow evidence, not the headline revenue target.
